<title>UK: London gold closes off lows, silver charges higher.</title>
<headline>London gold closes off lows, silver charges higher.</headline>
<text>
<p>GOLD - Ends down at $349.20/$349.70, vs $350.90/$351.40 on Wednesday after fixing at fresh 40-month low of $348.00. But off day's lows as silver surges.</p>
<p>SILVER - Rallies strongly on fund buying in PM to finish at $4.88/$4.90, up 16 cents. Gold/silver ratio narrows to 72.</p>
<p>PLATINUM - Up slightly at $356.25/$357.25, up $0.35.</p>
<p>PALLADIUM - Ends barely changed at $121.00/$122.00.</p>
</text>
